## Why Do We Skip Duplicate Elements?

### Skip Duplicate First Element

```java
if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) {
    continue;
}
```

After sorting, duplicate values become adjacent.

Without this check, the algorithm would generate the same triplets multiple times.

### Skip Duplicate Left Pointer

```java
while (left < right && nums[left] == nums[left - 1]) {
    left++;
}
```

Avoids storing duplicate triplets caused by repeated values.

### Skip Duplicate Right Pointer

```java
while (left < right && nums[right] == nums[right + 1]) {
    right--;
}
```

Prevents duplicate triplets from the right side.

